# Contributing

## Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture Engineering Repository – Public (AER-PU)

---

## Purpose

The purpose of this document is to establish the standard process for contributing engineering knowledge to the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture Engineering Repository – Public (AER-PU).

It ensures that every published contribution is reviewed, traceable, consistent, and aligned with the engineering philosophy and governance of the AVIA project.

---

# Contribution Philosophy

Engineering knowledge is considered a strategic asset of the AVIA project.

Every contribution shall improve the quality, consistency, traceability, or completeness of the engineering knowledge base.

Contributions are accepted based on engineering merit, not on contributor identity.

---

# Contribution Objectives

This contribution framework exists to:

- Maintain engineering quality.
- Preserve repository consistency.
- Support structured engineering collaboration.
- Ensure engineering traceability.
- Encourage continuous improvement.
- Protect repository integrity.

---

# Eligible Contributions

The repository accepts contributions including, but not limited to:

- Engineering specifications
- System requirements
- Architecture documents
- Engineering principles
- Engineering laws
- Technical reports
- Validation documents
- Engineering diagrams
- Repository documentation
- Engineering corrections and improvements

---

# Contribution Workflow

Every contribution shall follow the engineering lifecycle:

Proposal

↓

Preparation

↓

Engineering Review

↓

Revision

↓

Approval

↓

Baseline Assignment

↓

Publication

↓

Repository Maintenance

---

# Engineering Review

Every contribution shall undergo engineering review before publication.

The review shall evaluate:

- Engineering accuracy
- Consistency
- Traceability
- Completeness
- Alignment with repository governance
- Alignment with AVIA engineering philosophy

---

# Approval

Only approved contributions shall become official repository documents.

Approved contributions shall receive:

- Document Identifier
- Version Number
- Baseline Status
- Publication Status

---

# Traceability

Every contribution shall maintain traceability whenever applicable.

Engineering statements should be traceable to:

- Engineering objectives
- Engineering principles
- Approved requirements
- Previous engineering decisions
- Established baselines

---

# Contribution Standards

Every engineering contribution should:

- Be clearly written.
- Be technically accurate.
- Be solution-independent whenever appropriate.
- Use consistent engineering terminology.
- Support the overall AVIA architecture.
- Respect repository governance.

---

# Revision Policy

Engineering knowledge evolves continuously.

Contributors are encouraged to improve existing documents through controlled revisions rather than replacing historical engineering knowledge.

Previous approved versions shall remain preserved as part of the repository history.

---

# Repository Integrity

The repository prioritizes quality over quantity.

Engineering knowledge shall be published only after appropriate review and approval.

The objective is to maintain a repository that remains reliable, trustworthy, and valuable throughout the lifecycle of the AVIA project.

